2f:["$","details","Do I need to visit your office to register a business?",{"className":"group","id":"general-faq-4","name":"general-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Do I need to visit your office to register a business?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"No. Company and LLP incorporation is filed online with the Registrar of Companies, and digital signatures are issued through video and Aadhaar-based verification, so the process can be completed remotely from anywhere in Gujarat. Documents are exchanged digitally. You are welcome to visit us in Vadodara if you prefer to discuss things in person."}]}]]}]
30:["$","details","Can I change my business structure later?",{"className":"group","id":"general-faq-5","name":"general-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Can I change my business structure later?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Yes. A proprietorship can be moved into a partnership, LLP or company, a partnership firm can convert to an LLP or a company, and an LLP can convert to a company, each subject to conditions in the relevant law. Conversion is not free: it means new registrations, new bank accounts and updating vendor and customer records, so it is worth getting the choice roughly right at the start."}]}]]}]
31:["$","details","Is Raulji Group a government agency?",{"className":"group","id":"general-faq-6","name":"general-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Is Raulji Group a government agency?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"No. Raulji Group is a private business-services firm. We are not a government department and are not affiliated with the Ministry of Corporate Affairs, the GST department or any other authority. We prepare and file applications on your behalf, and approval always rests with the relevant authority."}]}]]}]
32:["$","details","What is the minimum capital required?",{"className":"group","id":"pvt-registration-faq-4","name":"pvt-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"What is the minimum capital required?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"There is no minimum paid-up capital requirement. The earlier ₹1 lakh threshold was removed by the Companies (Amendment) Act, 2015. You choose an authorised capital figure at incorporation, which affects the government fees and stamp duty payable rather than any money you must deposit."}]}]]}]
33:["$","details","What documents are required?",{"className":"group","id":"pvt-registration-faq-5","name":"pvt-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"What documents are required?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"PAN, Aadhaar, identity proof, recent address proof in the applicant's own name and a photograph for each director and shareholder, plus proof of the registered office address, a rent agreement if the premises are rented and a no-objection certificate from the owner. Foreign nationals need a passport with documents notarised or apostilled as applicable."}]}]]}]
34:["$","details","How long does registration take?",{"className":"group","id":"pvt-registration-faq-6","name":"pvt-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"How long does registration take?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Where documents are complete and the proposed name is approved on the first attempt, incorporation commonly completes in about 7 to 12 working days. Name rejections, resubmission requests from the Registrar and MCA processing volumes can extend this, so the figure is an estimate rather than a commitment."}]}]]}]
35:["$","details","How much does registration cost?",{"className":"group","id":"pvt-registration-faq-7","name":"pvt-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"How much does registration cost?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Our professional fee for Private Limited Company registration is ₹9,999. Government filing fees and stamp duty are payable in addition and depend on the state of the registered office and the authorised share capital. We confirm the full expected figure in writing before any filing begins."}]}]]}]
36:["$","details","Can a foreign national be a director?",{"className":"group","id":"pvt-registration-faq-8","name":"pvt-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Can a foreign national be a director?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Yes. A foreign national or NRI can be a director and can hold shares, provided at least one director on the board is a resident of India. Foreign directors need a valid passport and identity and address documents that are notarised or apostilled in line with the requirements of their country of residence. Foreign shareholding also attracts FEMA reporting obligations."}]}]]}]
37:["$","details","Can a startup register as a Private Limited Company?",{"className":"group","id":"pvt-registration-faq-9","name":"pvt-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Can a startup register as a Private Limited Company?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Yes, and it is the structure most startups use, because it is the only one of the four that can issue equity shares, create an ESOP pool and take investment on a priced or convertible basis. A Private Limited Company can also apply for recognition under the Startup India scheme once incorporated, subject to that scheme's own eligibility conditions."}]}]]}]
38:["$","details","What happens after incorporation?",{"className":"group","id":"pvt-registration-faq-10","name":"pvt-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"What happens after incorporation?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"The company opens a current account and the subscribers pay in their subscription money. The first auditor must be appointed within 30 days through Form ADT-1, and Form INC-20A declaring commencement of business must be filed within 180 days. From there the company files its annual ROC returns and financial statements and has its accounts audited each year."}]}]]}]
39:["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"What are designated partners?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}]
3a:["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Designated partners are the partners specifically responsible for the LLP's compliance obligations, including its ROC filings. They must hold a DPIN and a digital signature. Every LLP needs at least two, and at least one must be resident in India. Ordinary partners share in profits and management without carrying that statutory responsibility."}]}]
3b:["$","details","What documents are required?",{"className":"group","id":"llp-registration-faq-5","name":"llp-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"What documents are required?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"PAN, Aadhaar, identity proof, recent address proof in the partner's own name and a photograph for each partner, along with proof of the registered office address, a rent agreement if the premises are rented and a no-objection certificate from the owner."}]}]]}]
3c:["$","details","What is the LLP registration process?",{"className":"group","id":"llp-registration-faq-6","name":"llp-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"What is the LLP registration process?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Digital signatures are obtained for the designated partners, the name is reserved through RUN-LLP, the FiLLiP incorporation form is filed with the Registrar, the Certificate of Incorporation is issued with an LLPIN, and the LLP Agreement is executed on stamp paper and filed in Form 3 within 30 days of incorporation."}]}]]}]
3d:["$","details","Is the LLP Agreement mandatory?",{"className":"group","id":"llp-registration-faq-7","name":"llp-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Is the LLP Agreement mandatory?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Yes. The LLP Agreement must be filed in Form 3 within 30 days of incorporation. If no agreement is filed, the default provisions in the First Schedule to the LLP Act apply, which divide profits and management rights equally regardless of what the partners actually intended."}]}]]}]
3e:["$","details","How is an LLP different from a Private Limited Company?",{"className":"group","id":"llp-registration-faq-8","name":"llp-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"How is an LLP different from a Private Limited Company?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"An LLP cannot issue equity shares or create an ESOP pool, which rules it out for venture funding. In exchange it carries lighter compliance: no board or general meetings, and audit only once turnover exceeds ₹40 lakh or contribution exceeds ₹25 lakh. A Private Limited Company requires a statutory audit from its first year regardless of turnover."}]}]]}]
3f:["$","details","How is an LLP different from a partnership firm?",{"className":"group","id":"llp-registration-faq-9","name":"llp-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"How is an LLP different from a partnership firm?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"A partnership firm under the Indian Partnership Act, 1932, is not a separate legal entity and its partners carry unlimited personal liability, including for each other's acts. An LLP is a body corporate with limited liability, and a partner is not personally liable for another partner's wrongful acts. An LLP must file annually with the Registrar of Companies, which a partnership firm does not."}]}]]}]
40:["$","details","What annual filings does an LLP have?",{"className":"group","id":"llp-registration-faq-10","name":"llp-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"What annual filings does an LLP have?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Form 11, the annual return, is due by 30 May each year, and Form 8, the statement of account and solvency, by 30 October. Both are due even in a year with no business activity. Accounts must be audited if turnover exceeds ₹40 lakh or contribution exceeds ₹25 lakh. Late filing attracts a per-day penalty that keeps accruing until the filing is made."}]}]]}]
41:["$","details","Is partnership registration mandatory?",{"className":"group","id":"partnership-registration-faq-4","name":"partnership-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Is partnership registration mandatory?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"No. The Indian Partnership Act, 1932, does not compel registration, and a firm can legally operate without it. However, section 69 prevents an unregistered firm or its partners from suing to enforce a contractual right against the firm or against a third party. In practice that means an unregistered firm cannot go to court to recover money a customer owes it, so we recommend registering."}]}]]}]
42:["$","details","What documents are needed?",{"className":"group","id":"partnership-registration-faq-5","name":"partnership-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"What documents are needed?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"PAN, Aadhaar, identity proof, address proof and a photograph for each partner, the partnership deed executed on stamp paper, proof of the firm's place of business, a rent agreement if the premises are rented, and a no-objection certificate from the owner."}]}]]}]
43:["$","details","What is the registration process?",{"className":"group","id":"partnership-registration-faq-6","name":"partnership-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"What is the registration process?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"The partners agree their terms, a deed is drafted and executed on stamp paper of the value prescribed by the state, the firm applies for its own PAN, and an application is filed with the Registrar of Firms for the state with the deed and supporting proofs. The Registrar issues a certificate of registration on approval."}]}]]}]
44:["$","details","How is a partnership firm different from an LLP?",{"className":"group","id":"partnership-registration-faq-7","name":"partnership-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"How is a partnership firm different from an LLP?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"The difference that matters most is liability. In a partnership firm the partners are personally liable without limit, including for the acts of the other partners. In an LLP, liability is limited to the agreed contribution and a partner is not personally liable for another partner's wrongful acts. An LLP is also a separate legal entity and can hold property in its own name, but it carries annual ROC filing obligations that a partnership firm does not."}]}]]}]
45:["$","details","Can a partnership firm be converted into an LLP or a company later?",{"className":"group","id":"partnership-registration-faq-8","name":"partnership-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Can a partnership firm be converted into an LLP or a company later?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Yes. The LLP Act and the Companies Act both provide routes for converting a registered partnership firm into an LLP or into a company, subject to conditions including the consent of all partners. Many firms start as a partnership and convert once the business grows or once limited liability becomes a real concern."}]}]]}]
46:["$","details","How is a partnership firm taxed?",{"className":"group","id":"partnership-registration-faq-9","name":"partnership-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"How is a partnership firm taxed?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"The firm is assessed to income tax as a separate entity at the rate applicable to firms, plus applicable surcharge and cess. A partner's share of the firm's profit is exempt in the partner's own hands because it has already been taxed in the firm, but interest on capital and remuneration received from the firm are taxable for the partner, and are deductible for the firm only within the limits set by section 40(b)."}]}]]}]
47:["$","details","Who should choose a proprietorship?",{"className":"group","id":"proprietorship-registration-faq-4","name":"proprietorship-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Who should choose a proprietorship?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"It suits a single owner starting small, where the business is not carrying significant liability risk and there is no plan to bring in partners or investors. Freelancers, consultants, local retailers and small service businesses commonly start this way. If you need limited liability or intend to raise funding, look at an LLP or a Private Limited Company instead."}]}]]}]
48:["$","details","What registrations may be applicable?",{"className":"group","id":"proprietorship-registration-faq-5","name":"proprietorship-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"What registrations may be applicable?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Udyam (MSME) registration, which is free and widely accepted as proof of the business. GST registration where turnover crosses the threshold or where the nature of supply makes it compulsory. Shop and establishment registration under state law for commercial premises. Beyond those, activity-specific licences such as FSSAI for food businesses, Import Export Code for import or export, and professional tax where the state levies it."}]}]]}]
49:["$","details","Is GST registration compulsory for a proprietorship?",{"className":"group","id":"proprietorship-registration-faq-6","name":"proprietorship-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Is GST registration compulsory for a proprietorship?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Not always. It becomes compulsory once turnover crosses the applicable threshold, and irrespective of turnover in certain cases including inter-state supply of goods and supply through an e-commerce operator. Thresholds differ for goods and services and by state category. Some proprietors register voluntarily because business customers require a GST invoice to claim input credit. We assess which applies to your specific activity before filing."}]}]]}]
4a:["$","details","What documents are needed?",{"className":"group","id":"proprietorship-registration-faq-7","name":"proprietorship-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"What documents are needed?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"The proprietor's PAN and Aadhaar, a photograph, proof of the place of business, a rent agreement if the premises are rented, a no-objection certificate from the owner, and bank details for Udyam registration."}]}]]}]
4b:["$","details","How do I open a current account for a proprietorship?",{"className":"group","id":"proprietorship-registration-faq-8","name":"proprietorship-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"How do I open a current account for a proprietorship?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Banks open a current account in the business name against the proprietor's PAN and Aadhaar together with proof that the business exists. Under RBI KYC norms most banks ask for two such proofs, which in practice means a combination such as Udyam registration plus a GST certificate or shop and establishment registration."}]}]]}]
4c:["$","details","How is a proprietorship taxed?",{"className":"group","id":"proprietorship-registration-faq-9","name":"proprietorship-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"How is a proprietorship taxed?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Business income is included in the proprietor's own income tax return and taxed at the individual slab rates applicable to them, rather than at a separate rate for the business. There is no separate return for the business. A tax audit becomes applicable once turnover crosses the threshold under section 44AB, and presumptive taxation under sections 44AD or 44ADA may be available depending on the nature and scale of the activity."}]}]]}]
4d:["$","details","Can a proprietorship be converted into a company or LLP later?",{"className":"group","id":"proprietorship-registration-faq-10","name":"proprietorship-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Can a proprietorship be converted into a company or LLP later?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Yes. A proprietor can incorporate a Private Limited Company or an LLP and transfer the business to it, or form a partnership by bringing in a partner. This is a common path once the business grows, takes on more risk, or needs to look incorporated to its customers and lenders."}]}]]}]
